t number of times.\n`WeatherClient.get` now retries when the server returns 503, making at most 3 attempts in total. I checked it against a local test server and it behaves as intended.\n\n**What changed** (`weather.py`):\n- When a request gets a 503, it waits and tries again. The waits double each time (0.5s, then 1.0s), so the full delay before giving up is about 1.5s.\n- If the third attempt also gets a 503, the error is raised to the caller as before.\n- Any other HTTP error (for example 500) and network or timeout errors are raised right away, with no retry.\n- Two new optional constructor arguments, both with defaults, so existing callers don't need to change:\n  - `backoff=0.5` sets the first wait in seconds.\n  - `sleep=time.sleep` lets tests replace the real wait so they don't pause.\n\n**Test results** (fake `sleep`):\n\n| Server behaviour | Result | Requests | Waits |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 200 on first try | data returned | 1 | none |\n| 503, 503, then 200 | data returned | 3 | 0.5, 1.0 |\n| 503 every time | 503 error raised | 3 | 0.5, 1.0 |\n| 500 | 500 error raised | 1 | none |\n\nI didn't add a test file because the project has no test suite.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 6, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 104440, "requests_cache_write": 108496, "requests_cost_usd": 0.600484, "requests_count": 6, "requests_input_uncached": 14, "requests_output": 1853, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-netclient:claude-opus-5-5:trial23", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 105, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-20T03:51:24.626202+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 22.675, "t_checker_s": 4.89, "t_env_setup_s": 0.0, "task": "trig-omp-netclient", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "off", "thinking_sent": ["none", "n